 funding that we generate for ourselves  and not simply rely upon government  grant which is pretty much how we've  received it in the past so that's a  mixture that's a mixture of business  rates and again it's essential therefore  that we have a strong local economy to  make sure that those business rates  continue to be increased in a way that  allows us to reinvest them back into our  places  it's council tax and inevitably our  council is very keen on making sure that  we protect our residents as far as  possible from any kin  tax increases or significant council tax  increases and so more than ever before  it's about how we as local government  can generate new money generate our own  funding and so you'll see from some of  our achievements investing in things  like solar PV has meant not only a huge  return in terms of the environment but  it also brings in cash and so those  kinds of activities have become much  more the bread and butter of local  government now every penny we earn we  reinvest directly back into our  communities the more money we've got  clearly the more we can do for our  communities so we have a unique  challenge for Weber amid suffer because  we've made the decision that we're going  to move out of the two districts in  terms of our headquarters so will be  based predominantly in Ipswich and that  along with other reasons means that we  do have as it were a mini point in time  where you could say well what is it to  be Weber amid stuff again if you're not  even based in the two districts so we  need to work hard to create a brand for  the two district councils the private  sector is very good at that you get a  very clear sense when you think of  particularly multinational or local  companies you name a few such as John  Lewis or virgin or any others and you  immediately get a sense of what it is to  perhaps work for them what it is that  they believe in and what it is that  they're trying to achieve  whereas in local government we  traditionally haven't focused in that  area we haven't thought about those  those terms as it were and yet the  reason more important for me  the sense of what does Weber and what  does mid Suffolk believe in outside of  our politics is critical because we  govern in the same way that the police  policed by consent we govern by consent  and the decisions that our councillors  make on a day-to-day basis are only as  good as the trust and the confidence  that our communities and our residents  can place in those decisions so trust  for me is essential and we can't just  ask people to just this we have to  demonstrate what we believe in and so  brand and values are critically  important and those are certainly things  I expect us to be working on over the  course of the next 12 months or so as  well as obviously our normal day-to-day  job  you  [Music]
 

